"author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED reproduced locally (with fastapi installed): the test failed exactly as CI — 'Left contains 1 more item: {queue_depth: 0}'. Fix: corrected the exact-match assertion to the full intentional /health shape {status, in_flight, queue_depth}. GREEN: all 90 review_bot tests pass; lint + typecheck clean. Committed 161767febb (rebar-ticket + DCO + Change-Id I8a9551478e), on current origin/main 45ad7d3ece. Pushed as Gerrit change 1532.","timestamp":1786151536940747001}],"created_at":1786150475207424001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8a303ba4-4fd7-4c3b-a745-4537a97f07d4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181"},{"link_uuid":"82f6a8d5-7934-4d73-8a27-293d951214ff","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0fa0-1fd8-8c7b-473d"},{"link_uuid":"dba24de9-4acf-4c26-b08a-41c4e4de515a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0be9-eff3-d4e8-4d42"}],"description":"## Broken base: `/health` lifespan test asserts a stale exact dict (missing `queue_depth`)\n\n`origin/main` HEAD is **red on CI** (ubuntu py3.12, wherever `fastapi` is installed) due to a\nsemantic conflict between two independently-landed Gerrit changes:\n\n- `2bda965db6` (**9f63**) added `queue_depth` to the `/health` response body — intentional and\n  documented (`src/rebar/review_bot/app.py:274`):\n  `return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"in_flight\": _voter.in_flight_reviews(), \"queue_depth\": queue_depth}`\n- `4c89592d88` (\"test: make review-bot lifespan safe\") added\n  `test_lifespan_is_safe_by_default_without_per_test_stubs`\n  (`tests/unit/test_review_bot.py:1449`) asserting **exact** equality:\n  `assert response.json() == {\"status\": \"ok\", \"in_flight\": 0}` — missing `queue_depth`.\n\nEach change passed `Verified +1` in isolation; Rebase-If-Necessary submitted them without\nre-running the combined suite, so the merged tip fails. It skips locally when `fastapi` is\nabsent (why neither author caught it).\n\n**This deterministically fails EVERY change's CI**, so it must be fixed on `main` before any\nin-flight change (fc0c change 1528, etc.) can earn `Verified +1`.\n\n### Fix\nThe endpoint's `queue_depth` key is intentional (bug 9f63); the test's exact-match assertion is\nstale. Update the assertion to include the intentional key:\n`assert response.json() == {\"status\": \"ok\", \"in_flight\": 0, \"queue_depth\": 0}`.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- AC1: `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py::test_lifespan_is_safe_by_default_without_per_test_stubs`\n  passes with `fastapi` installed.\n- AC2: The assertion accounts for all three intentional `/health` keys (`status`, `in_flight`,\n  `queue_depth`) — no key dropped, no behavior changed in `app.py`.\n- AC3: No other review-bot test regresses.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0be9-eff3-d4e8-4d42"],["relates_to","0fa0-1fd8-8c7b-473d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a18b8328-0f37-4d28-915d-b5e1faa86b26","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0485-464a-86ab-464b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Fix stale /health lifespan test blocking all CI","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e8e33c39-548f-48eb-ba45-7314199847f5","8a303ba4-4fd7-4c3b-a745-4537a97f07d4","a18b8328-0f37-4d28-915d-b5e1faa86b26","4a25a4e5-4704-468c-963b-2e722d901a25","c675fb96-b8f2-4107-87ca-db3c142a7ebb","82f6a8d5-7934-4d73-8a27-293d951214ff","dba24de9-4acf-4c26-b08a-41c4e4de515a"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786152368138733096,"uuid":"26f09828-5c9d-4400-a28f-32096862f80b"}